Well, the main goal is to stave off the introduction of Uzi's, bazookas,
and other tools for those who think the game is too tough without them.
The basis of the game is still built around the weaponry of AD&D.

>Neither yo-yos nor shopping
>malls would stray from the current flavor of the game and would only 
>add to the fun.

Granted, but when the option exists to create a setting more consistent
with the groundwork of the game, like a village faire or a farmer's
market with city guard patrols, then there is some esthetic value in
going with the more Medieval setting.  BTW, there has been a yoyo-like
toy, consisting of a spindle spun by a string with ends tied to two
sticks for hundreds of years, so the yoyo is not too anachronistic,
anyway.

>If the consensus is that nethack should be stuck 
